.env
# Backups of the real .env also contain credentials. `.env` alone does not match
# `.env.bak-20261002-011629`, so a plain `git add -A` would publish the keys.
# `.env.example` stays tracked: the pattern is narrow on purpose.
.env.bak*
data/cache.db
data/cache.db-journal
data/raw/
data/graph/
eval/report.md
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.env
